{"kind":"report","text":"Approved for fixture-only A2 at f6e94550ecbde2f60042e9a74f75680e7000d995, tree 3aef23a0e5e7e206ef6897ff9ec45ce19b067a8b. No required changes found.\n\nCoverage: primary f16 read FIRST and FULL (167 lines); all 35 current, unretired path bindings reconciled. Reviewed the complete change from Main6e, new readers/adapters/ports/CLI, changed manifests/guards/tests and relevant unchanged native verification and A1 primitives. Independent extraction verified every one of 2,052 Git blob IDs, all 35 changed paths and 2,017 unchanged carried leaves; whitespace clean. Preparation and implementation notes are checkpoint narratives; the signed Source annotation and d45 gate record state the later exact-head result.\n\nArchitecture: the accepted b503 boundary is implemented. Git owns explicit-format object/layout validation and hardened local processes, with no Replay edge. Portable Replay adapts a trusted structural port and keeps native judges unchanged; the source-only Node composition and command supply separate file ports. Exact named SDK exclusions preserve the six-package boundary. My independent portable-root traversal visited 117 first-party files and found no Git/Node composition; the existing release module witness passed once in my scratch copy, and three added relative JS/dynamic/declaration closure probes refused. This was a static/source and synthetic-stage check, not a newly compiled or published SDK.\n\nSecurity: clone objects are checked by ID, type, size, canonical layout, scope/incarnation, contiguous position and hash chain before native verification. Unsafe tree modes/grammar are refused without opening archive paths as files. Local Git receives fixed validated argv, explicit environment/protocol hardening and bounded output/process lifetime; owned I/O is drained before return. Caller texts and receipts use bounded regular-file reads; detached text is serialized to native retained JSON and digest-checked. Receipt membership requires